WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501
-Congratulations.
Last time you were here we were

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.802
actually talking about this film
right before it came out.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, it hadn't.
No one had seen it.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nobody had seen it.
I'd seen it, I'd loved it,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now it turns out a lot
of people love it.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's starting to win
early awards

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
this first wave of awards.
-Yes, very exciting.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was Jordan Peele,
the director,

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.349
who a lot of people before this
knew from "Pee &amp; Keele,"

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fantastic comedy show.
-"Key &amp; Peele."

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Key &amp; Peele."
What did I say?

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Pee &amp; Keele?"
-Yeah, you good?

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I'm good.
-Okay.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.456
-I've taken a lot
of cold medicine over the course

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this week and sometimes
it makes my brain melt.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's cumulative, yeah,
I got it.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's okay, I'm here.
-Okay, thank you.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're welcome.
-But the movie is very heavy

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
at times, obviously.
Not only is it a horror movie,

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
but talks about race a lot.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.670
-But there's also great moments
of levity.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on top of that,
because Jordan is so funny,

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would direct in character,
is this true?

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
So, the movie is heavy.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not scary
to shoot a scary move,

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:50.884
which I learned doing this.
It feels like anything else.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone was like,
"Were you scared?"

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:54.387 line:92%
And I was like, "No, of Jordan?

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.188 line:92%
No, I wasn't scared of him."

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the scenes got heavy.
And there was this one scene

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
in particular,
this dinner conversation

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:03.129 size:84% position:42%
that's very fraught.
And at a certain point,

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to be laughing
at the beginning.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.734
We had been shooting it for
so long and Jordan can tell

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we weren't
laughing anymore.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were just like,
"Ha-ha-Ha-Ha-Ha!"

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it was just
not convincing anybody.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so he started directing us
as Obama, and that helped.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does a fantastic
Obama impression.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The best Obama impression,
in my opinion.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when that
stopped working,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he was about
to leave office,

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it was started
to get dark again.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he started doing
Tracy Morgan.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's the right order.
Yeah.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which was perfect.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.163
-So then, he directed us as
Tracy Morgan and then eventually

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.934
we broke through the, like,
tiredness and became slap-happy.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he was
about reigning us in.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's perfect.
-And he came back to Jordan.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.005
But there are perks to being
directed by a comedic genius...

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A sketch comedian.
-Yeah, exactly --

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.276
When you're doing, like,
really serious, you know,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.945 line:92%
not-so-funny organically stuff.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was an issue when you were
on this show,

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:56.182
was it an issue when you did
press leading up to before

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody saw it?
-Yeah.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because there was
a lot of spoilers.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, I think
of any horror film,

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
but particularly
your character.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So I do want to talk about

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.592
this now.
We are going to put up for those

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
who still haven't seen it,
first, shame on you.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're going to put up
a spoiler alert.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
So just turn down the volume
and when this goes away,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.032 size:81% position:41%
you can watch again.
-And we won't make any

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
hand signals that give
anything away.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:15.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, exactly.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it turns out you're
a bad guy.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I am.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, really bad.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.046 line:92%
-Like really, really bad.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the worst people
I can imagine.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:31.718
-Yeah, I think it's hard to
imagine you playing someone

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
more evil than you played
in this film.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know if I'll ever
be able to do it,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:39.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she literally is
a white supremacist

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
who eats cereal with the milk
and the cereal separate,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I just --
I think that might be

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
our world's worst person.
-Yeah, that is.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You're combining the two

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.836
worst things that are currently
happening.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.670 line:92%
-By the way, kind of a bummer.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.905
I can no longer eat Fruit Loops
in public.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:55.241
-Yeah, that's true.
-It just freaks people out now.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you actually --
I know some magazine did

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.813 size:78% position:39%
a list of things they
can't trust anymore

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
after the film came out.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.617 size:84% position:42%
-And you made the list.
-Yeah, I made the list.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not my character.
I am on that list.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:07.954 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.523 size:84% position:42%
They can't trust me.
And I don't blame them.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't blame them.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll just -- I might send him
a copy of "Peter Pan"

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be like, "Eh?"
-You know? Yeah, right.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that's true.
A lot of people --

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.999
That shows your great range that
you can do Peter Pan,

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:20.733 size:78% position:39% line:92%
who never turns evil.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he doesn't get old enough
to become evil.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-He's just flying and --

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.706
-But have you had people come up
to you and talk to you about

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.108
your character and actually try
to justify --

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
First of all, they stay about

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
this far away.
-Okay.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just because, you know --
you never know.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.114 size:84% position:42%
-You never know, right?
-Now I get that kind

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
of reaction.
And as Marnie, they did, too,

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.918
because they worried I was going
to judge or yell at them

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
or both.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.721
So I'm kind of used to that.
But yeah, they would say, like,

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
"She was hypnotized, right?"
And I'm like, "No.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's just evil.
How hard is that to accept?

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.362
She's bad."
We gave you so many ways to know

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she's bad.
She has photos of people

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose lives she ended
behind her.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
The minute she can,
she hangs them back up

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the wall behind her.
That's so crazy.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And they're still like,

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.573 line:92%
"But maybe she's also a victim?"

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "No! No!"

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's --
I will say, that is

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:06.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
100% white people that say
that to me.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.114 line:92%
-Yeah, I was going to guess.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:11.618
I was going to guess.
-It was very divided, but yeah.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I recently did --
I talked to Jordan

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the 92nd street Y where
we've talked before.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.759
It was funny because we were
talking about whether or not

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
the movie is a comedy.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:24.163
-And he was saying black people
think it's hilarious.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, well, also Lil Rel is
so funny as Rod.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.670
I mean, it is kind of confusing.
I've now been --

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.172
We've been doing these Q and As
and stuff so I've spent a lot

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
of time outside of a theater
playing "Get Uut."

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.977
So I, like, know what it sounds
like based on the audience.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.647
So I know that one of the cheers
is when I die.

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.347 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Thank you very much.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know one of the cheers
for each of my family members

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.552
and I'm so sorry if any of
you guys haven't seen it.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.222 line:92%
This is terribly inappropriate.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:49.922 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, anyways --
-Yeah.

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:53.293 line:92%
And then, but there's laughter.

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:55.862
So I can track where we are
based on how much laughter

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.196
there is, when they're cheering.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it is weird.
It's hard to put in a thing,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.667
which Jord--
that was the whole idea is that

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's kind of every genre
in one movie.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.604
-I also -- I want to compliment
your performance,

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.506 size:75% position:38%
because I've seen it
multiple times now.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the first time, you miss
a lot of the things

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were doing, because,
of course, you're the actor,

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:15.114
you know that you're actually
an evil person the whole time.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.451
When you watch it again,
you obviously were working

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.253 line:92%
to lay in, like, warning signs.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.789
-Yeah, I was trying to.
And the nice thing is that a lot

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people get lulled into
the sense of, like,

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:27.827
"Oh, she's just being as
racially aware as she can.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's doing her best.
She's got this evil family."

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:33.366
And then it just, you know,
when she refuses to cough up

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
the keys it, like,
hits them with a --

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like a weight is
falling on them.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.471 line:92%
But when you watch it again,

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:42.608
hopefully if I've done my job
right, every smile looks weird.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every look I give someone
looks evil.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:47.714
And some of that is just because
you know what you didn't then.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.916
And some of it, though, was
because Jordan and I worked

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.585
really hard on that, to try to
make everything look different.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's different motives
for everything.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, she doesn't want
the cop to take his ID because

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.991
she doesn't want to leave
a paper trail for where

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.862
she's taking this guy.
Or, you know, when her dad says,

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:05.531
"My mother loved this kitchen so
we kept a piece of her in here,"

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.967
and then it pans to reveal
Georgina, like the piece

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
they kept is her brain
in Georgina's body.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:16.542
Again, if you haven't seen t
his move, I cannot imagine what

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.810 line:92%
you are thinking right now.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are having a full
extensional crisis.

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:23.216
-I also realize we said we were
going to leave the spoiler up

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.951 size:78% position:39%
and we left it up for
the entire interview.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-So, I'm going to take it

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:27.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
down now.
Take down spoiler alert.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's all as it appears.
-As it appears.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:31.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I think this isn't

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
a spoiler alert.
Happy Holidays.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, Happy Holidays.

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's always so great
to see you.

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.930 line:92%
I'm so happy to have you here.

